  "note": "TWO lawful re-expressions of every record in the point's band window, neither moving the road, changing its length or altering which traversals are legal: `subdivide` inserts every segment's midpoint, and `split_midpoint` expresses each record as two cut at its arclength midpoint, and `split_every_segment` makes every segment its own record. All three are reported because they penalise different conventions -- reporting only the first would be choosing the transformation that makes the incumbent look worst. Drawn at RANDOM with the seed below; the first version took a prefix, which on the two censuses is id or row order and so a spatial bias, and a rate from a biased slice is not a rate. Kept out of the population estimates above: this is a transformation diagnostic on its own sample.",
